---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="PDTF 1.0"
  description="The published PDTF 1.0 schema implementation and derived semantic artefacts, each with its own status and maturity."
>
  <PageMeta category="PDTF 1.0" variant="info" updated="Published implementation · status varies by artefact" />
  <h1>PDTF 1.0</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    PDTF 1.0 is the published schema implementation and the semantic corpus derived from
    it. It remains directly findable for implementers while the programme continues into
    SPDTF 2.0 development.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">Read the status carefully</p>
    <p>
      The PDTF 1.0 label does not grant inherited authority to every child artefact.
      Individual ontologies, models, mappings and stubs retain their own maturity and
      review status. No replacement has been authorised, and this page does not define a
      support period.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="contents">Two parts of PDTF 1.0</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-1/original-standard" title="Original standard" eyebrow="Part one" description="JSON Schemas and overlays, data dictionary, business glossary, implementation guidance and adoption evidence." />
    <GatewayCard href="/ontology" title="Extracted PDTF 1.0 ontology" eyebrow="Part two" description="The ontology derived from those artefacts, with model views, qualified mappings, provenance and known limitations." />
  </div>

  <p>
    Implementers can go directly to the <a href="/schema">Schemas and overlays</a> or
    <a href="/implementation">Implementation guidance</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="continuation">Continuation into SPDTF 2.0</h2>
  <p>
    Existing dictionaries, glossary entries, documentation, schemas and mappings are
    attributed evidence for the next modelling method. Schemas can inform compatibility,
    constraints, coverage and migration; they do not determine new domain identities or
    relationships simply because those meanings were encoded in a document tree.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/spdtf-2">Read the SPDTF 2.0 development method</a> or
    <a href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/evidence-and-mappings">trace how evidence and mappings are qualified</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="legacy">Retained routes</h2>
  <p>
    Existing <code>/pdtf/**</code>, schema, ontology, mapping, model, implementation and
    adoption routes are retained inputs and implementation views. They are not moved,
    deleted or redirected by this gateway.
  </p>
</Layout>
